 "answer_text": "Found 1 disease record for Marfan syndrome: Marfan syndrome [12]. \n\nClinical Features\n\nMedGen lists these clinical features: Aortic regurgitation [1], Arachnodactyly [2], Astigmatism [3], Ectopia lentis [4], Esotropia [5], Exotropia [6], Pes planus [7], Glaucoma [8], Congestive heart failure [9] and Hypertropia [10]. These features span cardiovascular, skeletal, and ocular systems, consistent with the characterization of Marfan syndrome as a multisystem connective tissue disease with diverse clinical manifestations [11]. \n\nMarfan syndrome is mainly caused by FBN1 gene mutation and follows autosomal dominant inheritance [11]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Marfan syndrome [12]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Marfan syndrome [13]. Pubmed title: [Latest advances in the diagnosis and treatment of Marfan syndrome] [77]. Pubmed title: What Is Marfan Syndrome [79]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [81]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [83]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Marfan syndrome [14]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Marfan syndrome\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Aortic regurgitation [1]. Medgen clinical_features: Arachnodactyly [2]. Medgen clinical_features: Astigmatism [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Ectopia lentis [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Esotropia [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Exotropia [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Pes planus [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Glaucoma [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Congestive heart failure [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypertropia [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Micrognathia [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral regurgitation [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral valve prolapse [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Myopia [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Pneumothorax [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Emphysema [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Retinal detachment [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Retrognathia [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Scoliosis [23]. Medgen clinical_featur